<article class="env-lemma" id="09RT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09RT">Lemma <span data-tag="09RT">76.6.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ Z \ar[r]_ i \ar[d]_ f &  X \ar[d]^ g \\  Z' \ar[r]^{i'} &  X' }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a cartesian square of algebraic spaces over $S$ with $i$, $i'$ immersions. Then the canonical map $f^*\mathcal{C}_{Z'/X', *} \to \mathcal{C}_{Z/X, *}$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/09RS" data-tag="09RS">76.6.3</a> is surjective. If $g$ is flat, then it is an isomorphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We may check the statement after étale localizing $X'$. In this case we may assume $X' \to X$ is a morphism of schemes, hence $Z$ and $Z'$ are schemes and the result follows from the case of schemes, see Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/0635" data-tag="0635">31.20.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>